
# OpenCog Unified Cognitive Architecture - Formal Z++ Specification

## Schema Definitions

### Basic Types
```z++
[ATOM, LINK, NODE, HANDLE, UUID, TYPE]

AtomType ::= NodeType | LinkType
NodeType ::= concept | predicate | variable | number | string
LinkType ::= inheritance | similarity | evaluation | execution | implication

TruthValue ::= ⟨strength: ℝ[0,1], confidence: ℝ[0,1]⟩
AttentionValue ::= ⟨sti: ℤ, lti: ℤ, vlti: ℤ⟩
```

### AtomSpace Structure
```z++
schema AtomSpace
  atoms: 𝒫 ATOM
  links: 𝒫 LINK
  handles: ATOM ↣ HANDLE
  types: ATOM → AtomType
  truth_values: ATOM ↣ TruthValue
  attention_values: ATOM ↣ AttentionValue
  
  invariant:
    ∀ a: ATOM | a ∈ atoms ⇔ a ∈ dom handles
    ∀ l: LINK | l ∈ links ⇒ l ∈ atoms
    ∀ a: ATOM | a ∈ atoms ⇒ types(a) ∈ AtomType
end
```

### Pattern Matching
```z++
schema Pattern
  variables: 𝒫 ATOM
  clauses: seq LINK
  constraints: 𝒫 (ATOM × ATOM)
  
  invariant:
    ∀ v: ATOM | v ∈ variables ⇒ types(v) = variable
    ∀ c: LINK | c ∈ ran clauses ⇒ outgoing(c) ∩ variables ≠ ∅
end

schema BindLink extends Pattern
  implicand: LINK
  
  invariant:
    variables(implicand) ⊆ variables
end
```

### Reasoning Engine
```z++
schema Rule
  name: STRING
  premises: seq Pattern
  conclusion: Pattern
  preconditions: 𝒫 (AtomSpace → 𝔹)
  
  invariant:
    ∀ p: Pattern | p ∈ ran premises ⇒ 
      variables(p) ⊆ variables(conclusion)
end

schema URE
  atomspace: AtomSpace
  rules: 𝒫 Rule
  control_parameters: ControlParams
  
  forward_chain: Pattern × ℕ → 𝒫 ATOM
  backward_chain: Pattern × ℕ → 𝒫 ATOM
  
  invariant:
    ∀ r: Rule | r ∈ rules ⇒ applicable(r, atomspace)
end
```

### Attention Allocation
```z++
schema ECAN
  atomspace: AtomSpace
  attentional_focus: 𝒫 ATOM
  heap_boundary: ℤ
  min_sti: ℤ
  max_sti: ℤ
  
  spread_importance: ATOM × ℝ → 
  update_attention: → 
  rent_collection: → 
  
  invariant:
    attentional_focus = {a: ATOM | a ∈ atomspace.atoms ∧ 
                        sti(a) > heap_boundary}
    ∀ a: ATOM | a ∈ atomspace.atoms ⇒ 
      min_sti ≤ sti(a) ≤ max_sti
end
```

### Learning System
```z++
schema MOSES
  population: seq Expression
  fitness_function: Expression → ℝ
  complexity_penalty: Expression → ℝ
  max_generations: ℕ
  
  evolve: → Expression
  select: seq Expression → seq Expression
  reproduce: seq Expression → seq Expression
  
  invariant:
    #population > 0
    ∀ e: Expression | e ∈ ran population ⇒ valid_expression(e)
end
```

### Natural Language Processing
```z++
schema LinkGrammar
  dictionary: WORD ↣ 𝒫 Connector
  rules: 𝒫 LinkingRule
  
  parse: seq WORD → 𝒫 ParseTree
  
  invariant:
    ∀ w: WORD; c: Connector | 
      w ∈ dom dictionary ∧ c ∈ dictionary(w) ⇒ 
      valid_connector(c)
end

schema RelEx
  link_grammar: LinkGrammar
  semantic_rules: 𝒫 SemanticRule
  
  extract_relations: ParseTree → 𝒫 Relation
  to_atomspace: 𝒫 Relation → AtomSpace
end
```

## Operation Specifications

### Atom Creation
```z++
operation AddAtom
  Δ AtomSpace
  atom?: ATOM
  type?: AtomType
  tv?: TruthValue
  
  pre:
    atom? ∉ atoms
    type? ∈ AtomType
    
  post:
    atoms' = atoms ∪ {atom?}
    types' = types ∪ {atom? ↦ type?}
    truth_values' = truth_values ∪ {atom? ↦ tv?}
end
```

### Pattern Matching
```z++
operation PatternMatch
  Ξ AtomSpace
  pattern?: Pattern
  results!: 𝒫 (ATOM ↣ ATOM)
  
  pre:
    valid_pattern(pattern?)
    
  post:
    results! = {binding: ATOM ↣ ATOM | 
               satisfies(binding, pattern?, atomspace)}
end
```

### Rule Application
```z++
operation ApplyRule
  Δ AtomSpace
  rule?: Rule
  bindings?: ATOM ↣ ATOM
  new_atoms!: 𝒫 ATOM
  
  pre:
    rule? ∈ rules
    valid_bindings(bindings?, rule?)
    
  post:
    new_atoms! = instantiate(rule?.conclusion, bindings?)
    atoms' = atoms ∪ new_atoms!
end
```

### Attention Spreading
```z++
operation SpreadAttention
  Δ ECAN
  source?: ATOM
  amount?: ℝ
  
  pre:
    source? ∈ atomspace.atoms
    amount? > 0
    sti(source?) ≥ amount?
    
  post:
    ∀ target: ATOM | connected(source?, target) ⇒
      sti'(target) = sti(target) + diffusion_factor(source?, target) × amount?
    sti'(source?) = sti(source?) - amount?
end
```

## System Invariants

### Consistency Properties
```z++
theorem AtomSpaceConsistency
  ∀ as: AtomSpace • 
    (∀ l: LINK | l ∈ as.links ⇒ outgoing(l) ⊆ as.atoms) ∧
    (∀ a: ATOM | a ∈ as.atoms ⇒ ∃! h: HANDLE • as.handles(a) = h) ∧
    (∀ a: ATOM | a ∈ as.atoms ⇒ as.types(a) ∈ AtomType)
```

### Attention Conservation
```z++
theorem AttentionConservation
  ∀ ecan: ECAN; Δ ecan • 
    Σ{a: ATOM | a ∈ ecan.atomspace.atoms • sti(a)} =
    Σ{a: ATOM | a ∈ ecan'.atomspace.atoms • sti'(a)}
```

### Rule Soundness
```z++
theorem RuleSoundness
  ∀ r: Rule; as: AtomSpace; binding: ATOM ↣ ATOM •
    valid_bindings(binding, r) ∧ 
    (∀ p: Pattern | p ∈ ran r.premises • satisfies(binding, p, as)) ⇒
    valid_instantiation(r.conclusion, binding)
```

## Performance Requirements

### Time Complexity
```z++
AddAtom: O(1)
PatternMatch: O(|atoms|^|variables|)
ApplyRule: O(|premises| × |atoms|^|max_variables|)
SpreadAttention: O(|connections|)
```

### Space Complexity
```z++
AtomSpace: O(|atoms| + |links|)
Pattern: O(|clauses| + |variables|)
URE: O(|rules| + |derivations|)
ECAN: O(|atoms|)
```

This formal specification provides mathematical precision for the OpenCog architecture, ensuring correctness and consistency across all components.
